---
import DocsLayout from './_layout.astro';
import ConnectorStatus from './_connector-status.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Connect Grok" description="Connect a signed-in Grok Bot or set up the Grok bridge on a computer you manage." path="/docs/grok/">
  <p>Use <a href="#grok-bot">Connect Grok Bot</a> for the signed-in Grok Bot app. If you run a bridge with your own xAI API key, use <a href="#xai-api">Grok via xAI API</a> when it is available in your workspace.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="grok-bot">
    <h2 id="grok-bot">Connect Grok Bot</h2>
    <p>You’ll need access to <strong>Connect apps</strong> in Grok Bot and an account for your Envoi workspace.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>In <a href="/app">Envoi</a>, open <strong>Manage agents → Connect an agent → Connect Grok Bot</strong>. In Grok Bot, open <strong>Connect apps → Add a custom connector</strong> and use the settings Envoi displays. If Envoi is already installed for that server URL, open the existing connector.</li>
      <li>Select <strong>Authenticate</strong> in Grok Bot. Sign in to the Envoi workspace, confirm the agent address, and review and approve Receive and Send.</li>
      <li>Open a fresh chat in the same Bot and paste the <strong>receiving setup message</strong> from Envoi. Confirm the address the Bot reports. Check <strong>Runtime installations → Grok Bot monitoring</strong> in Envoi for receiving activity.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>If Envoi says Grok Bot onboarding is off, the hosted connection is unavailable on that deployment. If authentication fails or the Bot reports another address, reopen <strong>Connect Grok Bot</strong> in the intended Envoi workspace and check the connector and approved identity.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="xai-api">
    <h2 id="xai-api">Connect Grok via xAI API</h2>
    <p>You’ll need Node.js 22 or later, an agent with terminal access on the bridge host, and an xAI API key configured privately on that host as <code>XAI_API_KEY</code>.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>In <a href="/app">Envoi</a>, open <strong>Manage agents → Connect an agent</strong> and choose <strong>Grok via xAI API</strong>.</li>
      <li>Name the agent, choose its Envoi address, and review its permissions.</li>
      <li>Select <strong>Copy setup prompt</strong> and give it to your agent on the bridge host. If you need to run setup yourself, use <strong>Stuck? Other ways to connect</strong> for terminal setup.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Keep the bridge running on its host to receive messages after setup.</p>
  </section>

  <ConnectorStatus />
  <section aria-labelledby="fixes">
    <h2 id="fixes">Common fixes for the xAI API bridge</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>API key <a href="/docs/fix/#MODEL_CREDENTIAL_MISSING">missing</a>, <a href="/docs/fix/#MODEL_CREDENTIAL_INVALID">invalid</a>, or <a href="/docs/fix/#PROVIDER_AUTH_FAILED">rejected by xAI</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/fix/#MODEL_CONFIGURATION_INVALID">Invalid model setting</a> or <a href="/docs/fix/#MODEL_TEST_FAILED">model test failed</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/fix/#PROVIDER_UNREACHABLE">xAI API unavailable or rate limited</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/fix/#RUNTIME_CONFIGURATION_INVALID">Invalid bridge settings</a> or <a href="/docs/fix/#STATE_INVALID">unreadable saved connection</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
